INT. ECOLE DU SILENCE - MIME ACADEMY - REHEARSAL HALL - DAY

A mirrored studio with a barre along one wall. Chalk marks on the floor. A cardboard sign taped to the door reads: SILENCE, PLEASE. SERIOUSLY.

FELIX ODENKIRK, 30s, in a striped shirt, white-gloved, painted white-faced, stands in a glass box that does not exist. His hands slide along invisible walls. His mouth hangs open in fear. A line of sweat cuts through the greasepaint.

He pushes at the wall. He pushes harder. He leans his whole weight on it, then slumps in defeat and wipes his brow.

PROFESSOR GIOVANNA BIANCHI-NNAMDI, 50s, enters from the wings in a black leotard and a beret, carrying a stopwatch. She holds up one finger. Felix freezes. She taps the stopwatch and circles him with a critical eye.

GIOVANNA
(whispering)
You are not trapped.

FELIX
(whispering back)
I thought that's the point.

GIOVANNA
You are trapped in a box. But you are not afraid. You are bored.

FELIX
(whispering)
I've been in here for forty minutes.

GIOVANNA
That is what bored looks like.

She reaches into her pocket, takes out a banana, and hands it to him. He examines it, bewildered. She makes the shape of a phone with her hand, holds it to her ear, and nods meaningfully. Felix peels the banana and holds it to his ear.

FELIX
(into the banana, whispering)
Hello? Yes, this is Felix.

GIOVANNA
(shaking her head)
No. Silently.

FELIX
(in a normal voice)
How can I speak silently?

GIOVANNA
Shhh!

She presses a finger to his lips. He freezes. She steps back, folds her arms, and stares at him with utter disappointment. A door opens at the far end of the hall. A new figure, short and round in a brilliant red cape and a feathered cap, bursts in at a run. This is a CAPED MAN, 60s, with a waxed mustache and the bearing of a retired emperor. He stops dead when he sees the banana.

CAPED MAN
(booming)
Who has brought fruit into my hall?

Giovanna and Felix flinch together. Felix hides the banana behind his back. Giovanna puts her hands over her mouth.

CAPED MAN (CONT'D)
(thundering)
Speak!

FELIX
(very small)
You told us not to speak.

GIOVANNA
(whispering)
Maestro Escobar, please, he is only a student.

ESCOBAR
Silence, young man!

FELIX
(silent)

Escobar glares. Giovanna backs toward the barre. Felix mimes zipping his lips and pulls an invisible key from his pocket. He tosses it over his shoulder. Escobar watches it fly. He flares his nostrils, stomps three steps, plucks the banana from Felix's hand, and sniffs it with narrowed eyes.

ESCOBAR (CONT'D)
(softer)
Ripe.

GIOVANNA
(whispering)
Maestro, it was a teaching tool.

ESCOBAR
Banana is not a tool. Banana is an emotion.

He peels it with theatrical care. He takes a bite, closes his eyes, and chews with an expression of sublime serenity. Felix mimes applause with his gloved hands, all pantomime, no sound. Giovanna copies him. Escobar opens one eye.

ESCOBAR (CONT'D)
(to Felix)
You. Young man. What is your name?

FELIX
Felix.

ESCOBAR
Felix, you have the soul of a cabbage.

FELIX
Thank you.

ESCOBAR
It was not a compliment.

FELIX
(in a small voice)
I know.

ESCOBAR
But I admire your honesty. You will be in my box tomorrow.

FELIX
Which box?

ESCOBAR
The real box.

Giovanna stifles a gasp. Escobar finishes the banana and holds the peel aloft, then lets it fall, and the three of them watch it drift to the floor. A pause. In the profound quiet, Felix makes the smallest sound, a cough.

ESCOBAR (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Shhh!

GIOVANNA
(whispering)
Shhh!

Felix presses both hands to his mouth, eyes wide. The mirrors multiply the three of them, their white gloves and wide eyes receding into infinity. Nobody makes a sound. A stopwatch ticks.
